 "title": "A member edited on a PC: TAB characters between words and trailing white space",
 "category": "reference-format",
 "issue": null,
 "realism": "Members that went through a PC editor (or a git-hosted estate) carry TABs and trailing blanks or TABs. Mainframe source has none; GnuCOBOL and modern toolchains accept them.",
 "shapes": [
  "PCED PCEDTAB: a TAB after the first word of every Area B line; ' <TAB> ' or two blanks at the end of every third line"
 ],
 "asserts": "A TAB between words is white space (a separator) and trailing white space is nothing: every fact is what the member says with the TABs read as blanks.",
